WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.940
Sphinx, Jackalope, Manticore, Griffin, Hippogriff.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.730
All monsters made up of body parts from more
than one animal.

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:16.789
We now call these hybrid monsters chimeras,
owing to the original Chimaera of ancient

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:17.789
Greece.

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:24.099
A ridiculously impractical mythological monster,
with three heads: a lion, a goat, and a snake,

00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:29.210
which seems absurd, but then again, humans
have been crafting these mythological creatures

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.660
for thousands of years.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.000
In more ways than one.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.699
When I say humans have crafted Chimeras for
thousands of years...I mean hand crafted.

00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:48.980
As in sewing dead bodies together.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.359
The Ancient Romans displayed a “centaur”
preserved in honey.

00:00:52.359 --> 00:00:56.650
The figure was likely made from mummified
human and horse remains.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:02.219
The Romans also exhibited a puppet with a
false human head attached to a large serpent

00:01:02.219 --> 00:01:06.110
that could open and close its mouth and flick
its snake tongue.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:07.430
It fooled quite a few people.

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:12.609
And don’t even get me started on all the
weird taxidermy trends in the Victorian period

00:01:12.609 --> 00:01:13.609
.

00:01:13.609 --> 00:01:16.950
But it’s not all jumbled up animals, and
antlers glued to rabbits.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:22.920
A real, living chimera of a sheep and a goat--a
“geep”--was made in the 1980s.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:27.310
Now I could try to explain all of this, and
do a terrible job at it, but I’ll turn to

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:28.561
the esteemed Dr. Joe Hanson.

00:01:28.561 --> 00:01:31.049
Joe, can you help me out here?

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:32.920
Ok, maybe you’ve heard of ligers?

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:33.920
Mules?

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:34.920
Beefalos?

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.790
Zonkeys, coydogs, wholphins, or maybe pizzly
bears?

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:42.540
Those are all real examples of two animals
combined into one.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.090
But they’re not chimeras, biologically speaking.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:50.479
They’re hybrid animals, one embryo that
came from two related species mating, like

00:01:50.479 --> 00:01:52.390
a lion and a tiger.

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:54.939
But the geep was different.

00:01:54.939 --> 00:02:00.350
That started with two embryos, one goat and
one sheep, that were combined to make one

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.460
embryo.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:04.600
Two bodies or embryos combined into one?

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.450
That’s a chimera.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:07.590
SCIENCE!

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:13.610
So scientists refer to these animals as chimeras,
a concept with its roots deep in mythology.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:16.990
Mythical hybrid animals have existed in cultures
around the world for centuries.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:21.330
It wasn’t until Homer’s Iliad, that the
word “chimaera” first appears.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:26.750
Here, The Chimaera is a female “beast”
with the “upper body of a lion, the tail

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:29.840
of a snake, and a goat head in the middle
of its torso.”

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.750
A fire-breathing goat head.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:37.630
Yeahhh, it has three heads and the goat is
the most threatening one.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:43.130
In the story, Bellerophon is ordered to kill
the Chimaera, a seemingly impossible task.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:48.680
Luckily for our hero, his noble steed is none
other than the winged horse Pegasus, which

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:50.640
helps him kill the Chimaera from above.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:51.640
Pegasus?

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:55.170
Also, a chimera - lower case “c” chimera.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:56.210
Go figure.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:03:00.960
After Homer’s tale, other Greek writers
followed with their own versions of the Chimaera

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:01.960
story.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:07.570
Most set Chimaera’s home in Lycia; 500 long
miles from Athens, a metaphor for the Greeks’

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:11.390
fear of the foreign, and what they saw as
“uncivilized” territory.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:16.250
It’s also a place known for mysteriously
burning ground fires caused by natural gas

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:21.590
leaking to the surface, but to humans of the
time, a fire breathing goat was just as likely.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:25.900
The mountain where these fires burned was
appropriately called Mount Chimaera.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:30.660
So how the heck do we explain the inspiration
for the lion/goat/serpent heads thing?

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:35.930
[Joe] We don’t see actual animal chimeras
in the wild, but we do sometimes see certain

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:40.550
traits on one species that kind of appear
to come from other species?

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:46.530
Like extra limbs, or how some humans have
extra fingers that make them look kinda reptile-y.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:51.510
And during development, many vertebrate embryos
pass through stages that resemble more ancient

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:57.700
branches of life, like fish, complete with
gill-looking growths… so that would be confusing

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:58.830
in olden dayes.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:03.400
And finally, some animals can be born with
multiple heads… though they’re always

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:09.100
the same kind of heads, so you gotta stretch
the scientific truth to get to mythical chimeras.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:13.970
One explanation for the creation of this odd
three-headed creature might come from human

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:16.400
confusion of early fossil discoveries.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:21.170
It’s possible that the fossilized bones
of a goat, a lion, and a snake could have

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:25.460
been found in the same place, when they were
killed by a flash flood or fell into a tar

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:31.180
pit., Humans discovered their fossilized remains
together, and imagined a Chimaera to explain

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.180
what they saw.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:37.170
There is a ton of ancient art that depicts
the Chimaera, everything from coins and statues

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.140
to containers and plates

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:43.590
Because of its presence in The Iliad and other
Classical Greek texts and art, the Chimaera

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:47.590
continued to be a recognizable myth as the
centuries wore on.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:52.580
The word “chimaera” came to signify not
just a hybrid animal but any thing that seemed

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:55.690
to be impossible or a figment of the imagination.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:05:00.670
Only over the last few decades have we been
able to accept, and prove, that interspecies

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:02.530
chimeras are possible.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:07.690
After the “geep,” another crazy moment
in chimera history happened in 1998 when two

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:13.100
scientists tried to get a patent on a variety
of human-animal chimeras.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.920
And yes, they used that term specifically.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:21.110
The patent was rejected as an invention that
would be “injurious to the well-being, good

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:26.280
policy, or good morals of society,” and
the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office commissioner

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:30.670
reportedly even referred to these proposed
creations as “monsters.”

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:34.460
But research into human-animal chimeras continues.

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:38.440
Some scientists are growing human tissues
inside pigs in order to one day improve how

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:39.800
we transplant organs.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:43.640
But the ethics and feelings surrounding this
kind of research are… complicated.

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:47.950
I mean, in a world of human-animal chimeras…

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.400
What constitutes a human?

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:54.230
If I grew bird wings, would I be considered
a human or a chimera?

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:59.710
As technology advances, the possibility of
even human chimeras becomes real.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:04.800
The world of biological chimeras is even weirder,
so head over to Its Okay to be Smart and watch

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.920
Joe’s video to learn about that.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:08.850
So we’ve come full circle.

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:13.600
From the impossible Chimaera monster of Greek
mythology to the potential for real animal

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:14.600
chimeras.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:20.160
When we move from the realm of fantasy into
reality, things get much more complicated.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:24.860
So it’s no longer just an exercise of imagination
but a question about ethics.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:28.000
We can craft chimeras, but should we?

